Independent research and consulting practice focused on geospatial
modeling, AI for cities, and open-source urban analytics.

This product includes software and data developed for the paper of the
same title. Code, documentation, annotation guides, claim-level labels
and derived result tables are released under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Third-party data and content redistributed or referenced in this
repository carry their own terms, which are unaffected by the Apache
License:

  * The three frozen spatial briefs (briefs/*.json) contain indicator
    values derived from OpenStreetMap data retrieved on 25 June 2026.
    (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

  * Population figures in the briefs are derived from GHS-POP R2023A,
    European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC), released under
    CC BY 4.0. doi:10.2905/2FF68A52-5B5B-4A22-8F40-C41DA8332CFE

  * Reverse-geocoded place names were obtained from Nominatim
    (OpenStreetMap data, ODbL 1.0).

  * The raw model outputs (benchmark/runs/**/*.jsonl) and the claim
    sheets derived from them were generated with open-weight language
    models whose weights are distributed under their own licences:
    Qwen3 (Alibaba Cloud, Apache 2.0), Gemma 3 and Gemma 4 (Google,
